Carry agent status on the headless session-tab surface

Toggling an agent tab from terminal to chat in the tile showed the empty "Start
a chat with Claude" state, the model picker read a bare "Model", and the pane
blanked again on every toggle - while the same agent's transcript renders on
desktop and on a phone paired to a desktop server.

A desktop host feeds every paired client by hanging its store's
`AgentStatusEntry` off each session-tab surface, which the client mirrors under
its own pane key. `orca serve` has no renderer store, so the headless builder
omitted the field and all three symptoms followed from that one gap. The field
is resolved from the host's agent-hook rows at `toMobileSessionTabsResult`, the
single publish boundary every client-visible result passes through - not at any
of the eleven producers, because `mergeMobileSessionSnapshotTabs` keeps the
cached tab and would freeze or drop a value stamped at build time.

To test, restart the workspace, open an agent pane in the tile and toggle to
chat: the prior transcript and the model name should appear with no hook event
fired, and survive toggling back and forth. Covered by
`headless-agent-status-surface.test.ts` and
`agent-status-session-surface.test.ts`.

